<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 84,785 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 84,785 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 84,785 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 48,978 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   April 22</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 7,140	 3,452</p>
<p>    Import cargo		77,645	45,526</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, nine are expected to sail and 11 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to</p>
<p>unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	 18,600	 Tula			23/4</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 New Tatina		23/4</p>
<p>Crude oil	    70,000	 Stavros-I		 24/4</p>
<p>Palm oil		6,200	 Wawasan Megah	   25/4</p>
<p>Palm oil		8,600	 Wawasan Courage	 25/4</p>
<p>Rock phosphate     22,000	 Artemis-II		25/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
